What is a VPC in AWS?
    VPC = Virtual Private Cloud.
    A VPC is a logically isolated virtual network inside AWS where
    you can launch AWS resources such as EC2 instances, databases, load balancers, etc.

Why do we need a VPC?
    The main purpose is network isolation and control.
    You control things such as:
        IP address ranges
        Subnets
        Routing
        Internet access
        Security Groups
        Network ACLs
        Connectivity to other VPCs or on-premises networks
